! The Mana Lifts

''Kind:'' Routes (the vertical pointcrawl network) · ''Scale:'' Nexus-wide.

Canon: ''mana lifts near the major Lares landmarks'' join the ports of High Delos and Low
Delos — and since the gradient left islands half-aloft ("half a town up, half at anchor"), the
lift-traffic threads the whole constellation: sky-hub to ring-port to crater-town. On-lift
travel runs as Route procedure — timetable and toll, no navigation.

''The open ruling — who keeps the lifts:'' League charter · a Lift-Wardens' guild · the Order
of Amaranth · or the Lares landmarks themselves as literal route-keepers. The keeper of a Route
holds a hand on every throat in the Nexus; the referee's choice here writes half the Nexus's
politics.

